#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &systemsettings; provides the user with a centralized and convenient way "
"to configure all of the settings for your desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&systemsettings; is made up of multiple modules. Each module is a separate "
"application, however the &systemsettings; organizes all of these "
"applications into a single location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each &systemsettings; module can be executed individually"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See section entitled <link linkend=\"run-modules-individually\">Running "
"individual &systemsettings; modules</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&systemsettings; groups all of the configuration modules into several "
"categories:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"appearance\">Appearance</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"workspace\">Workspace</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"personalization\">Personalization</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"network\">Network</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"hardware\">Hardware</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The modules that make up &systemsettings; fall under one of the above "
"categories, making it easier to locate the correct configuration module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &systemsettings;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section details the use of &systemsettings; itself. For information on "
"each individual module, please see <link linkend=\"modules"
"\">&systemsettings; Modules</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &systemsettings;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &systemsettings; can be started in one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>System "
"Settings</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the <guilabel>Application Menu</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By pressing <keycombo>&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>. This will bring "
"up the &krunner; dialog. Type <command>systemsettings</command>, and press "
"&Enter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type <command>systemsettings5 &amp;</command> at any command prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "All three of these methods are equivalent, and produce the same result."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &systemsettings; Screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &systemsettings;, you are presented with a window, which is "
"divided into three functional parts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Across the top is a toolbar. The toolbar provides the user with the ability "
"to go back into the main view from within a module using the "
"<guibutton>Overview</guibutton>. You can also find a <guimenu>Help</guimenu> "
"menu as well as a <guibutton>Configure</guibutton> button which provides you "
"a dialog with alternate view settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To search for something within all of the modules, start to type keywords "
"into the search field at the right of the toolbar in the "
"<guibutton>Overview</guibutton>. When you start typing, a list of matching "
"topics will popup. Select one and only the groups with settings for this "
"keyword are enabled, the other are greyed out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the icon window has the focus, you can type the first letter of any "
"module or module group name to select it. Typing this letter again the "
"selection moves to the next match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Underneath the toolbar is an icon view of the individual modules or module "
"groups that make up &systemsettings; grouped by different categories. By "
"default, if your mouse stays a few seconds over an icon, a detailed tooltip "
"appears, explaining the purpose of the module or the modules in this group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "&systemsettings; Categories and Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "A brief overview of all categories and their modules:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Appearance</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Workspace Theme (Look and Feel, Desktop Theme, Cursor Theme, Splash Screen)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font (Fonts, Font Management)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icons (Icons, Emoticons)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Application Style (Window Decorations, Widget Style, GNOME Application Style "
"(GTK))"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Workspace</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Desktop Behavior (Workspace, Desktop Effects, Screen Edges, Virtual "
"Desktops, Accessibility, Activities)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Window Management (Window Behavior, Task Switcher, KWin Scripts, Window "
"Rules)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shortcuts (Application Keyboard Shortcuts, Global Keyboard Shortcuts, Web "
"Shortcuts, Custom Shortcuts)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Startup and Shutdown (Autostart, Background Services, Desktop Session, Login "
"Screen (SDDM))"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search (Plasma Search, File Search)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Personalization</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Account Details (Password &amp; User Account, KDE Wallet)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Regional Settings (Translations, Format, Spell Check, Date &amp; Time)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Applications (Default Applications, File Associations, Paths, Launch "
"Feedback)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Network</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings (Proxy, Connection Preferences, SSL Preferences)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Hardware</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Human Input Devices (Keyboard, Mouse, Joystick)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display and Monitor (Compositor, Screen Locking)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multimedia (Audio and Video)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Power Management (Energy Saving, Advanced Settings)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Device Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the search field at the top right in <guibutton>Overview</guibutton> to "
"find all matching modules for a given keyword. Start typing a keyword opens "
"a list of keywords and only the matching modules are enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exiting the &systemsettings;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "&systemsettings; can be exited in one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Press <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> on the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guibutton>Close</guibutton> button located in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &systemsettings;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guiicon>Configure</guiicon> icon in the toolbar allows you to change "
"some &systemsettings; parameters. You can change from <guilabel>Icon View</"
"guilabel> (default view) to <guilabel>Classic Tree View</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also turn off the detailed tooltips by unchecking <guilabel>Show "
"detailed tooltips</guilabel>. You will then get only normal tooltips and not "
"the content of a module group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Running Individual &systemsettings; Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Individual modules can be run without running &systemsettings; using the "
"command <command>kcmshell5</command> from the command line. Type "
"<command>kcmshell5 --list</command> to see a list of the available "
"&systemsettings; modules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &systemsettings; Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to make it as easy as possible, the &systemsettings; has organized "
"options into five categories. Under each category, there are icons grouped "
"together under subcategories. Each icon is called a module. When you double "
"click on a module icon, you will be presented with the options of the module "
"in the main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each module will have some or all of the following buttons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will provide help specific to the current module. Clicking the "
"button will open &khelpcenter; in a new window providing detailed "
"information on the module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore Defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking this button will restore this module to its default values. You "
"must click <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> to save the options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reset"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will <quote>Reset</quote> the module to the previous settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking this button will save all changes. If you have changed anything, "
"clicking <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> will cause the changes to take effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must either <quote>Reset</quote> or <quote>Apply</quote> the changes "
"before changing to another module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you try to change without saving or resetting your options, you will be "
"asked if you want to save your changes, or discard them."
msgstr ""

